WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.594
Planning connects the observation objective to a safe and lawful method.

00:00:05.594 --> 00:00:16.558
Review the location, applicable rules, airspace, property access, terrain, obstacles, people, nearby operations, and current official restrictions before selecting a route or platform.

00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:21.704
Weather and lighting affect both aircraft safety and evidence quality.

00:00:21.704 --> 00:00:28.640
Wind, visibility, precipitation, temperature, glare, cloud cover, and shadows may change during the mission.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:33.787
Select conditions that fit equipment limitations and the analytical question.

00:00:33.787 --> 00:00:39.380
Identify a controlled launch and recovery area when using a drone.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:44.527
Plan battery margins for takeoff, collection, return, contingencies, and landing.

00:00:44.527 --> 00:00:51.911
Do not build a route that depends on ideal endurance or an uninterrupted communication link.

00:00:51.911 --> 00:01:00.637
Design a flight path or observation sequence that covers the authorized area with the required angle and overlap.

00:01:00.637 --> 00:01:05.336
Keep unnecessary private areas outside the frame where practical.

00:01:05.336 --> 00:01:10.035
Mark decision points for returning, landing, or ending collection.

00:01:10.035 --> 00:01:20.103
Prepare emergency options for changing weather, low battery, signal loss, people entering the area, navigation problems, or an unavailable recovery point.

00:01:20.103 --> 00:01:25.250
Brief crew communication and define who can call a stop.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:33.976
Document objective, location, crew, platform, permissions, official-source checks, weather, lighting, hazards, controls, route, collection settings, and emergency actions.

00:01:33.976 --> 00:01:39.570
A written plan supports repeatability and later interpretation of the imagery.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:44.716
Review the plan immediately before collection because conditions can change.

00:01:44.716 --> 00:01:54.338
A route that was reasonable during desktop planning may become unsuitable when people, vehicles, glare, wind, or temporary activity appear.
